# =============================================================================
# i3c_target.pdc  -  Physical constraints for the I3C Target on Certus-NX
#
# No pin locations: the block is built as an IP core and Radiant PAR places the
# ports automatically (see reports/pad.pad for what it chose). Add
# `ldc_set_location -site {<ball>} [get_ports <port>]` lines here for a real board.
#
# The only physical constraint is electrical and I3C-specific: Radiant's default
# for an unconstrained pad is PULLMODE=DOWN, and an internal pull-down on SDA/SCL
# would fight the bus pull-up / high-keeper whenever the line is released. Turn it
# off. OPENDRAIN stays OFF (default): the pad must also drive push-pull High.
# IO_TYPE is left at the tool default (LVCMOS33); set it to the bus voltage
# (LVCMOS18 / LVCMOS12) together with the bank VCCIO on a real board.
# =============================================================================
ldc_set_port -iobuf {PULLMODE=NONE} [get_ports SDA]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {PULLMODE=NONE} [get_ports SCL]
